## Pitfalls

- **Single-band "measurements".** One or two points cannot constrain T_dust (2015ApJ...807..180W,
  2015ApJ...813...45L). A fixed-SED L_IR carries about 0.2-0.3 dex systematics (2015MNRAS.453L..83M,
  2016MNRAS.461.2944A, 2020MNRAS.491.4724F) and up to a factor 2-3 for quasar hosts (2020ApJ...904..130V). Quote
  the assumed T and beta next to every number.
- **T-beta degeneracy.** Papers fit beta fixed and free (2019ApJ...879..117K, 2017ApJ...847...21F) or average two
  (T, beta) pairs (2017MNRAS.465.4390B: 47 K/1.6 and 41 K/1.95). Do not compare T_d across papers with different
  beta.
- **Optically thin vs thick.** The same data give 58.5 K or about 33 K (2014A&A...562A..67G). Say which.
- **Missing hot component.** A single cold MBB misses warm dust (2016MNRAS.463...10M admits this); include a
  mid-IR power law or drop rest <50 um points.
- **CMB at high z.** Ignoring CMB heating and contrast biases T and M_d (about a dozen dust papers' lines mention a
  CMB correction, my count; e.g. 2016ApJ...822...80S, 2017ApJ...850...83F, 2020ApJ...897L..14Y). Some papers state they skipped it
  (2015ApJ...807..180W).
- **Uncertainty budgets that leave things out.** L_FIR errors excluding T uncertainty (2013ApJ...770...13W);
  fit errors excluding absolute calibration (2021A&A...656A..46M); redshift errors propagated only through a
  grid, so errors are lower limits (2017A&A...597A...5M).
- **Opacity and mass factors of 2.** kappa choices differ by about 2x (0.077 vs 0.15 m2/kg at 850 um, see table);
  using Dunne et al. 2000 instead of Hildebrand doubles M_d (2019PASJ...71...71H); CIGALE dust masses were divided
  by 2 to match Draine07 opacities (2025A&A...694A..82S); opacity uncertainty alone is a factor 2
  (2014ApJ...791..108F).
- **AGN and synchrotron contamination.** SFR and gas mass are overestimated if AGN heating is not removed
  (2026ApJ..1001..131C); radio-galaxy mm continuum can be synchrotron (2016A&A...591A..73G).
- **Blending and deblending assumptions** that cannot be verified (2016A&A...596A..75S), and lensing with one
  magnification (2016ApJ...822...80S).
- **Unknown redshift.** Assuming z=2.5 makes those results "less reliable" (2017ApJ...844..123F).
- **Unstated settings.** In the pack's "not stated" list, the flux-calibrator / flux-scale-uncertainty variants
  sum to 33, as many as CASA version (33; my sum of the pack lines), and cards often note that SED
  code priors, grids and initial values are not given (e.g. 2017ApJ...844..123F, 2020MNRAS.493.3744F,
  2026ApJ..1001..131C). State yours.

## Verification checks

What papers did:
- Refit with the parameter free that you fixed and confirm it comes back: T_cold free recovered 35 K
  (2014ApJ...790..160S).
- Compare optically thin vs general-opacity fits and report the spread (2014A&A...562A..67G,
  2017ApJ...844..123F, about 0.1 dex in L_IR).
- Cross-check codes: CIGALE vs MAGPHYS (2026ApJ..1001..131C), CIGALE as a sanity check of templates
  (2016A&A...596A..75S), MBB vs MAGPHYS within about 0.5 dex (2020A&A...633A.160C), L_IR vs Draine07 within 10%
  (2020A&A...642A.155Z).
- Drop bands and refit: unchanged without Herschel (2016A&A...596A..75S), with and without SPIRE
  (2018ApJ...859...35G).
- Compare SFR_IR with independent SFRs: radio (2016A&A...596A..75S), SED-decomposition SFR vs FIR SFR
  (2014A&A...562A..67G).
- Report goodness of fit: median reduced chi2 0.52 (2024ApJ...962....1S); reduced chi2 of 1
  (2014ApJ...790..160S).
- Compare dust-based gas mass with CO-based and dynamical mass (2018Sci...362.1034D).

What a careful referee adds:
- A table of every input flux with its error, the error floor, and which points are limits.
- The full prior list and sampler settings; show T-beta posterior contours.
- L_IR in both 8-1000 um and 42.5-122.5 um with the conversion stated, and SFR with the IMF and constant.
- For single-band sources, the spread in L_IR over T_d = 25-50 K and beta = 1.5-2.0 (the ranges in the pack
  above), instead of one number.

