### Limitations the authors admit
- 2016A&A...596A..75S: Herschel fluxes of the SMG derived through indirect procedure with unverified assumptions; Y-band scatters ~2 sigma from best fit
- 2020A&A...633A.160C: Stellar masses below ~10^8.5 Msun likely incomplete; selection biases at low mass
- 2020A&A...633A.160C: Stacked values biased toward high-weight sources
- 2014A&A...562A..67G: Size measurement needs confirmation at higher resolution; sparse uv sampling
- 2026ApJ..1001..131C: A3COSMOS gas masses do not include AGN contribution; AGN may bias gas mass of 195616
- 2018ApJ...859...35G: Systematic uncertainty in outflow mass from alpha_CO
- 2018ApJ...859...35G: Extreme obscuration may hide AGN; mid-IR decomposition may be biased
- 2019ApJ...878..103R: Uncertainties are qualitative; selection effects make conclusions difficult; brightest disks may be atypical
- 2018ApJ...853..171G: Catalog potentially incomplete; completeness cannot be quantified
- 2018ApJ...853..171G: Column density maps not very accurate; SFR strongly dependent on assumed timescale
- 2018Sci...362.1034D: U1 may be at a different redshift; stellar mass and SFR uncertain by factor of 2
- 2021A&A...648A..41V: Outflow masses are lower limits (no correction for missing flux at cloud velocities or opacity); sample not statistically significant.
- 2024ApJ...962....1S: Mass outflow rate uncertainty dominated by poorly constrained OH abundance
- 2024ApJ...962....1S: Almost no line-free channels in USB; simple fitting assumptions
- 2016ApJ...818...45S: Putative 13-AU belt needs deeper data; SED models degenerate due to lack of Rayleigh-Jeans constraints
- 2014A&A...567A.125G: Outflow rate is a lower limit due to limited velocity coverage
- 2014A&A...567A.125G: Resolution does not resolve kinematics of inner r~50 pc
- 2015ApJ...801...82H: Missing flux and lack of short baselines; BN outside field of view; flux calibration unreliable for sources outside primary beam; no size correction in SED
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: Calibration uncertainty not included in fit uncertainties; line flux scaling anomalies in some tunings
- 2021A&A...656A..46M: STATCONT continuum subtraction not optimal for lines near noise level
- 2015ApJ...806L..22C: Low SNR and possible cloud contamination prevent constraining mass; gas content unconstrained
- 2024A&A...690A.185W: Missing flux: masses and column densities are lower limits
- 2015A&A...581A..97S: Axisymmetric discs only; models not unique
- 2018ApJ...853..195W: Optical selection of members may bias the star-forming census; small samples of CO detections.
- 2020ApJ...893..125U: Flux calibration uncertainties may be larger than official values; absolute opacity is uncertain.
- 2018A&A...614A..17B: Present-day mass-loss rate is poorly constrained and should be interpreted with care
- 2024ApJ...972..163L: Q band hard to calibrate and marginal; detailed spinning-dust model beyond scope
- 2020MNRAS.493.3744F: FIR SED poorly sampled so L_IR and SFR are lower limits; kinematics unresolved; SLED has too few points
- 2019ApJ...871...73H: Band 9 excess is only 2 sigma
- 2025A&A...698A.183D: ALMA resolution limits conclusions on the mm belt morphology
- 2019MNRAS.488..191G: Observations not simultaneous across radio, mm and IR; no firm conclusions
- 2014ApJ...790..160S: Outflow quantities order-of-magnitude; XCO and line ratio uncertain
- 2014ApJ...795L..25R: Core unresolved so density is a lower limit; deviation may be from temperature
- 2020AJ....159..288M: Coarse resolution; disk width fixed; contamination by faint background sources cannot be ruled out
- 2020AJ....159..288M: Dust opacity systematics not in error budget
- 2015A&A...576L..15O: Flux lost to missing short spacings; large uncertainties in masses and orbital estimates
- 2020ApJ...891..164S: Infall not detected because no optically thick tracer; NH2 includes low-temperature components
- 2024ApJ...962..116E: X-ray coverage limited to 1-10 keV
- 2025A&A...696A.100G: Exact chemical pathways and relative contributions of bottom-up and top-down processes remain unquantified; models omit PAH chemistry
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: X_CO uncertainty may overestimate molecular mass by a factor of a few
- 2024ApJ...963....1O: Chandra data too shallow to resolve cavity
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: Distance mismatch between GRS 1915+105 and IRAS source; jet power assumes constant power and density
- 2018MNRAS.475..448T: ALMA continuum lacks single-dish data so flux is underestimated
- 2023NatAs...7...80U: PA difference between radio and optical only ~90% significant
- 2017ApJ...844..123F: Redshifts of non-QSO SMGs unknown (assumed 2.5), making their results less reliable
- 2017ApJ...844..123F: Size measurements at SNR<10 are biased high
- 2017ApJ...844..123F: Duty cycle is an upper limit since no BH accretion assumed in SMGs without QSOs
- 2020A&A...642A.155Z: Single lines cannot give definitive redshifts
- 2014ApJ...788..125S: Stellar masses have systematic uncertainties up to 5x because SFHs are unconstrained
- 2024A&A...690A..55S: Halo mass estimates carry large uncertainties; group centre and concentration degeneracies; interloper contamination
- 2024A&A...690A..55S: Cold-stream regime scatter based on only six points
- 2017ApJ...851...98T: Peak S/N ~20 makes weak broad components hard to detect; FIR SED poorly constrained.
- 2017ApJ...840L..12S: Envelope mass and radius are degenerate; data cannot distinguish compact low-mass from large massive envelopes
- 2019A&A...626A..36D: DCF/SF values are order-of-magnitude; flux loss 30-70% from missing short spacings
- 2019A&A...626A..36D: Mass and column density errors could be factors of 5-10
- 2019ApJ...887...74F: Limited depth and resolution prevent distinguishing disk, merger and outflow
- 2019ApJ...887...74F: Dust mass depends strongly on the adopted kappa
- 2021A&A...653A.117B: Low statistics and poorly constrained temperatures hamper strong conclusions
- 2024A&A...684A..56K: Data not standardized, resolution limited, CO SLED turnover unconstrained
- 2016ApJ...828...25L: Low resolution prevents breaking R_Out/p degeneracy and resolving widths
- 2025ApJ...988..185G: Lack of high-resolution mid- to far-infrared data limits reliability of derived properties; near-IR PSFs unresolved for some.
- 2014ApJ...787...48X: Good map quality only in the central ~3'' due to uv-coverage; astrometric accuracy ~0.1''
- 2015A&A...577A..30A: MM1a free-free fit least robust as turnover may be above 25 GHz
- 2020A&A...633A.127F: Mass uncertainty dominated by assumed alpha and geometry; values are lower limits due to projection
- 2013Sci...341..630Q: Vertical disk structure is uncertain; vertical N2H+ boundaries fixed
- 2025ApJ...993..120H: Dust mass may be a lower limit if emission is optically thick
- 2025ApJ...993..120H: A closer unresolved binary cannot be ruled out
- 2015ApJ...798..124R: Data cannot distinguish between gap and double power-law forms; dust opacity degenerate with surface density
- 2018ApJ...862...64S: Small field and low-number statistics; field comparison selection not equivalent
- 2021AJ....161..238W: Midplane thermal emission not vertically resolved; smooth tapered density model too simple
- 2017ApJ...841..130A: Planned ALMA sensitivity not reached, so nebula undetected
- 2017ApJ...841..130A: Central-object size is an upper limit; flux systematics from differing beams and nebular contamination
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Short snapshot observations, lack of short spacings, gas radii as lower limits
- 2024ApJ...966...59S: Dust masses are lower limits if optically thick
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Common T_dust adopted for all sources; mass estimates depend on assumed conversion factors
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Spectral index maps only possible for 3 sources
- 2021A&A...652A..98G: Small-number statistics for orientation and correlations
- 2019ApJ...884L..58U: Non-simultaneous multi-wavelength polarimetry limits conclusions
- 2025A&A...693A.151M: Sample biased by flux-density limits; heights may be extracted from azimuthal profile rather than resolved
- 2016A&A...594A.107K: ALMA observations have 1-2 arcsec offsets from ICRS and were not designed for astrometry
- 2016A&A...594A.107K: S-star proper motions not statistically significant; nature of S stars poorly constrained by broadband photometry
- 2015ApJ...813...45L: Dust temperature unconstrained for most sources; L_BB and SFR uncertain by orders of magnitude
- 2015ApJ...808...97Y: SFR is only an order of magnitude estimate
- 2015A&A...577L...4V: Band 3 resolution too poor to confirm the hotspot there; 25 Oct Band 3 epoch affected by resolved calibrator
- 2019PASJ...71...71H: M_dyn uncertain by at least a factor of three; virial theorem may not apply.
- 2019PASJ...71...71H: Clump continuum fluxes may be contaminated by each other at current resolution.
- 2020ApJS..247...61F: Spitzer blending can overestimate stellar masses; about one-third have contaminated Spitzer photometry
- 2020ApJS..247...61F: f-factor is the largest uncertainty in the Halpha measurement
- 2015ApJ...807..180W: Single continuum point; dust temperature unconstrained
- 2025ApJS..278...45F: 1-2 sources may be spurious; no completeness correction for IRLF; z>9 detections marginal
- 2017MNRAS.468L..87C: Cold dust mass is only an estimate; alternative dust properties would change it
- 2018ApJ...860....7R: Resolution insufficient to fully resolve the inner disk
- 2018ApJ...866..141K: Source-X has too little visibility data for size analysis; Td assumed
- 2018ApJ...866..141K: Lack of redshifted counterpart for SM1-A outflow is puzzling
- 2019A&A...621A..27F: Upper limits dominate many SFRs; no intermediate-frequency data to determine synchrotron steepening
- 2020ApJ...902..141S: HOPS-56B envelope mass is more uncertain due to nearby source subtraction
- 2020ApJ...902..141S: HOPS-124 and HOPS-157 envelope masses may be lower limits
- 2024A&A...682A..54T: Resolution cannot distinguish merging from rotation, or single from multiple companions
- 2017ApJ...839...86H: Grid search does not characterize uncertainties on CO parameters
- 2025ApJ...995L..63L: delta_DGR concerns H2 only, ignoring atomic HI
- 2025ApJ...995L..63L: Mdust uncertain due to assumed Tdust and unknown AGN presence
- 2015MNRAS.450L..80B: Unidentified systematic amplitude calibration effects could affect flux densities
- 2015MNRAS.450L..80B: Attenuation analysis uses simple sheet model
- 2014ApJ...796...82Z: Equipartition estimates may be inaccurate for flat spectra; double-subtracted images unusable due to errors
- 2021ApJ...908...54W: Mostly upper limits on M_H2 and SFR preclude robust depletion time measurement
- 2021ApJ...908...54W: alpha_CO uncertainty of factor >=2
- 2015ApJ...812..126C: Absolute flux scale uncertain, affecting spectral index and optical depths
- 2024MNRAS.532.3625M: ALMA 315 GHz flux likely underestimated because of the small maximum recoverable scale
- 2013ApJ...777L..25M: Details of grain migration cannot be constrained by the data
- 2016ApJ...829...53V: ALMA source membership unconfirmed; it would double the core SFR
- 2020MNRAS.492.1531M: Grain size distribution may be biased to small sizes; dust mass and optical depth uncertain
- 2017ApJ...841..110S: Envelope size only a lower limit because CO is in absorption
- 2025ApJ...984L..19Y: CO/H2 ratio uncertain; absolute gas surface density scales as X_CO^-0.5
- 2025ApJ...984L..19Y: Dust opacity model uncertainty affects gas-to-dust ratio; limited spatial resolution
- 2020ApJ...897L..14Y: Black hole mass uncertainty excludes scaling-relation systematics of up to ~0.5 dex
- 2020ApJ...897L..14Y: Large uncertainties and a broad PDF for x_HI prevent solid conclusions
- 2019ApJ...878L..26L: Systematic uncertainties from RS dynamics approximations and stochastic random walk; forward-shock parameters degenerate since nu_a not located
- 2026ApJ..1004..182H: Aspect ratio poorly constrained; uncertainties large in inner disk and outer edge; small uncertainties exclude PSF-subtraction systematics
- 2017A&A...600A...8D: Observations not strictly simultaneous; 4U 1728-34 in transitional state
- 2018MNRAS.478.3721S: 14 CDF-S targets observed at too-high resolution, requiring heavy tapering and giving higher noise

