  - method: chi2 fit of optically thick modified blackbody to ALMA+Herschel+ATCA data [3 Far-IR SED: "A simple $\chi^2$ fit to the FIR SED of XID403 returns an acceptable statistics with a best fit temperature of $T_{\rm d}=58.5\pm5.3$K"]
  - assumption: beta=2 and lambda0=200 um fixed [3 Far-IR SED: "we fixed the dust emissivity index to $\beta=2$ and the rest-wavelength at which the dust becomes optically thick (i.e. $\tau_{\nu} =1$) to $\lambda_0=c/\nu_0=200\mu$m"]
  - fitting: chi2 minimisation [Far-IR SED: dust mass and temperature: "A simple $\chi^2$ fit to the FIR SED of XID403 returns an acceptable statistics with a best fit temperature of $T_{\rm d}=58.5\pm5.3$K"]
  - validation: Compared with optically thin fit (T~33 K) and literature SMGs [7.2 Dusty Star Formation: "we would measure a colder dust temperature $T_d\sim33$ K"]
- step 4: Derive L_IR, SFR and SFR surface density
  - method: Integrate best-fit greybody; Kennicutt98 SFR; Sigma_SFR=(SFR/2)/(pi r_half^2) [4 Star formation rate: "By integrating the best-fit modified greybody spectrum we obtained a far-IR (42.5-122.5$\mu$m) luminosity"]
  - assumption: Cosmology H0=67, Om=0.32, OL=0.68; 1 arcsec=6.6 kpc [1 Introduction: "A concordance $\Lambda$CDM cosmology with $H_0=67$ km s$^{-1}$ Mpc$^{-1}$, $\Omega_m=0.32$, $\Omega_{\Lambda}=0.68$"]
  - validation: Agreement with Coppin09 and Gilli11 [Star formation rate and compactness: "These values are in excellent agreement with those previously derived by (cite: coppin09) and (cite: gilli11) and have significantly smaller uncertainties."]
- step 5: Broad-band SED decomposition
  - method: Fit stellar, AGN torus and dusty SSP components to optical-FIR photometry [5 SED decomposition: "The optical to far-infrared (millimeter) data of XID403 were modelled using the spectral energy distribution (SED) fitting code originally developed by (cite: fritz06) and recently updated by (cite: feltre13)."]
  - software: Fritz06/Feltre13 SED code
  - assumption: Salpeter IMF, Calzetti attenuation, solar metallicity, z_form=8 [5 SED decomposition: "Extinction to the stellar component is modelled using a (cite: calzetti00) attenuation law."]
  - validation: Compared SFR with FIR-derived value [SED decomposition: "Once corrected for this contribution, the far-IR luminosity can be used to derive a star-formation rate of $\sim$1040 M$_{\odot}$/yr, in excellent agreement with what has been estimated in Section 4."]
- result: Dust temperature = 58.5 ± 5.3 K [Table 2: "| $T_{dust}$ | $58.5\pm5.3$ | K | this work |"]
- result: SFR = 1020 ± 150 Msun/yr [Table 2: "| SFR | $1020\pm150$ | $M_{\odot}$yr$^{-1}$ | this work |"]
- result: L_IR (8-1000um) = 5.9e12 ± 0.9e12 Lsun [Table 2: "| $L_{IR}$ | $5.9\pm 0.9$ | $10^{12} L_{\odot}$ | this work |"]
- result: Sigma_SFR lower limit = >26 ± not stated Msun/yr/kpc2 [Table 2: "| $\Sigma_{SFR}$ | $>26$ | $M_{\odot}$yr$^{-1}$kpc$^{-2}$ | this work |"]
- result: Stellar mass = 1.1e11 ± within 50% Msun [5 SED decomposition: "stellar mass $M_*\sim1.1\times10^{11}$ M$_{\odot}$"]
- limitation (authors): Size measurement needs confirmation at higher resolution; sparse uv sampling [2 ALMA observations: "this measurement needs to be confirmed by data at even higher resolution"]
- not stated (card): CLEAN parameters (weighting, robust, cell, size, masking); Flagging details and phase-calibrator solutions; Exact fit setup for uvmodelfit (starting values); Parameters of the SED decomposition fit beyond qualitative description; Photometry in the CANDELS fit and SPIRE 250um flux (Daddi et al. in prep)

### 2026ApJ..1001..131C: MAGAZ3NE: Far-IR and Radio Insights into the Nature and Properties of Ultramassive Galaxies at z ≳ 3 (2026; high_z_galaxies, agn_and_quasars; archival_reuse)
